# Possibility of creating edgeql function with conditional insert #1590
created: 2020-07-25, last updated: 2026-05-21, [Read more](https://github.com/geldata/gel/discussions/1590)

- Conditional inserts are not possible yet: SELECT Object IF EXISTS Object ELSE INSERT #684
...
Putting DML statements inside conditionals is not supported (aside from a specific case that is being worked on in #684), so you cannot do `DELETE foo IF condition ELSE ...`, instead you should put the deletion condition into the `FILTER` clause of the `DELETE` statement, like so:
...
This leaves conditional `INSERT`, and in this case it's not possible to express the delete-and-then-insert logic in a single query.
This is actually a Postgres limitation.
What *is* possible (with #684 in mind) is an `UPDATE`-or-`INSERT` to reuse the existing `User` object:
```
function create_user(nickname: str, email: str, pass: bytes) -> optional User
{
...
WITH
MODULE default
SELECT (
(
UPDATE User
FILTER
...
SET {
created_at := datetime_of_transaction(),
# ...
reset all other properties
}
)
??
# no users were updated, no conflict so INSERT
(
INSERT User {
nickname := nickname,
email := email,
password := password,
}
)
)
);
};

